# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dsh-code-reviewer - local environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` in the repository root for local runs:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit a real key. The CLI reads the key from the
# process environment first, then from `.env` in the current directory, then
# from `$DSH_HOME/.env` (see CONTRACT.md §2).
#
# GitHub Actions: create the key as a repository secret named DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
# (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret).
# Workflows never print the value. Fork pull requests do not receive repository
# secrets, so the review workflow skips the LLM and runs deterministic checks
# only for forks, while same-repo PRs FAIL LOUDLY when the secret is missing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required for any LLM-backed command (`review run`, `review all`, `review scan`,
# pre-push hook in "full" mode, the DSH plugin) and for the PR review workflow.
# Format: a DeepSeek API key (Anthropic-compatible Messages API).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Optional. Anthropic-compatible endpoint used by the default `anthropic`
# transport. Defaults to https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic when unset.
# For the OpenAI-compatible transport use https://api.deepseek.com (transport:
# "openai" in .review/config.json).
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic
